---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../config/site';
---

<Base title="Disclaimer" description="The terms of using TextKit tools: free, as-is, and your responsibility to verify results that matter." path="/disclaimer/">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Disclaimer</h1>
    <p>
      {SITE_NAME} is provided free of charge, "as is", for general-purpose text and data
      utilities. By using the tools you accept the points below.
    </p>
    <h2>Verify results that matter</h2>
    <p>
      The tools implement standard, well-documented algorithms (the JSON specification,
      RFC 4648 Base64, the SHA family, RFC 4122 UUIDs) and are tested, but no warranty is
      given that every output is correct for every input. If a result feeds a production
      system, a publication or anything with money or safety attached, check it with an
      independent method first.
    </p>
    <h2>Security-sensitive use</h2>
    <p>
      Hashes and generated passwords are produced with your browser's cryptographic
      functions. Even so, a hash is not encryption, Base64 is not protection, and a generated
      password is only as safe as where you store it — use a reputable password manager.
      {SITE_NAME} never sees your inputs, and equally cannot recover anything for you.
    </p>
    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent permitted by law, the operators of {SITE_NAME} are not liable for losses
      arising from the use of, or inability to use, these tools. External sites linked from
      guides or articles are the responsibility of their own operators.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
